Z||000011||isthiswhereiputausername?||10-01-2001||11:54 AM||||Before I started working on the fiero myself, I had a backyard mechanic "try" to install a 4banger motor I bought off him..<P>3 weeks later he was still trying to get the old one out..<BR>I got annoyed..<BR>I went to tow it home.. His son (my age) said he wont be home til late and I can come back tomorrow and get the car(he had the keys)<P>BAD MOVE LEAVING IT THERE THE EXTRA DAY!<BR>I towed the car home.. replaced the motor myself.. then had to replace it again the day after I got it started.. the F**KER put tons of crap in my gas tank..  <P>Insurance wouldnt pay for it either.. (they said sugar will not sieze a motor..only gum it up) the tank was packed with everything.. sugary type stuff,stuff that looked like molassas(sp?), TONS of sand.. <P>This guy has a very bad rep (I found out too late)<P>My advice.. get it out of there quickly and dont give him any warning of your plans..<P>show up with ability to move both cars at that time or have someone stay with the other car until you can come right back and get it..<P>||||reg||9
Z||000012||Alex4mula||10-01-2001||04:31 PM||||That's exactly how I learned to install a clutch/tranny in my Fiero. I disasembled the car with a "friend" mechanic of mine and he was looking for someone to fix the tranny. Every day he said that he did something here and there but when I went by his home everything was in the same position. One day I got tired of it and told him that I was going to relocate to other state and that needed to take the car (didn't want to hurt the relationship nor paying him any $$). Took tow truck and put the car home and did it myself. Never again went to him for work. Now I thank him for my Fiero mechanical abilities  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000013||Voytek||10-01-2001||05:16 PM||||Get the cars out and get them out now.<P>Been through a similar thing with a transmission shop (dinky, non-reputable garage).<P>'Oh, yes' they said, 'your new clutch will be ready for tomorrow, $800.00.<P>One, week and many phonecalls and visits later the car was done and I ended up paying $1300.  BBB can't do anything unless the shop is a member, i.e. you could get the cars back in little pieces and no one will help you.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000014||8Ball||10-01-2001||06:42 PM||||Ok I went to his shop for a FINAL confrontation. The hyundai as I said befor is in pieces. The Fiero is finally up on the racks. Part of the reason I took my cars to him is because he has been known around here to work on Fiero's. He was (supposedly) getting ready to work on my water leak. If nothing is done by tomorrow I will be getting my cars. I wish I had done it this morning but I was already running late for work, and with as much as I have missed due lack of transportation I couldn't really afford it. I am thinking about buying a couple of 4 cyl Fiero's at a good price and selling them or parting them out in order to try to get my finacial outlook back on track.<BR>Not sure if I wanna risk it though.<P>Anyway we shall see what happens tomorrow.<BR>Thanks everyone||||reg||1
